      },
      "type": "function"
    },
    {
      "description": "Edit text in files using literal search-and-replace. All non-no-op edits in a single call succeed atomically or none are applied. Edits with identical old_text and new_text are skipped.\n\nGuidance:\n- Always Read the file first before editing.\n- old_text must match exactly once in the file. Include 3+ surrounding lines for uniqueness.\n- For multi-line matches, preserve exact whitespace and indentation.\n- Special characters in JSON (backticks, quotes, backslashes) must be escaped.\n- Each successful edit invalidates any earlier read of that file. Re-read before editing the same file again.\n- The parameters are named old_text and new_text (not old_string/new_string).\n",
      "name": "Edit",
      "parameters": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "edits": {
            "description": "The edits to make to the file. Edits with identical old_text and new_text are no-ops; they are skipped and reported without changing the file. The max number of edits you can do at once is 20.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "new_text": {
                  "description": "Replacement text. Use empty string to delete",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "old_text": {
                  "description": "Exact text to replace. Must be unique in the file",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "old_text",
                "new_text"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            "maxItems": 20,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array"
          },
          "path": {
            "description": "The path of the file to edit",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path",
          "edits"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "type": "function"
    },
    {
      "description": "Read a file's contents. Returns line-numbered content. Supports reading specific line ranges to avoid loading large files entirely.\n\nBehavior:\n- Defaults to reading lines 1-200. Provide start_line/end_line for large files.\n- Returns a \"N more lines\" note when the file extends beyond the requested range.\n- Rejects binary files (null-byte detection).\n- Rejects directory paths (use Bash with ls, find, or tree for directory listings).\n\nWarning: Ranged and truncated reads return only the requested region. Do not compose old_text for an Edit from content outside the returned lines — the match will fail.\n",
      "name": "Read",
      "parameters": {
        "properties": {
          "end_line": {
            "description": "Last line to read (1-indexed, inclusive). Default: 200 (or start_line+199 when start_line given)",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "path": {
            "description": "Absolute path to the file to read",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "start_line": {
            "description": "First line to read (1-indexed, inclusive). Default: 1",
            "type": "integer"
          }
